      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A review of data reported in Soviet and foreign literature and the authors' own experience allowed specifying a number of clinical and angiographic criteria for the selection of coronary patients for surgical treatment. Clinical criteria include the pain syndrome, progressive angina pectoris, severe pain with a sharp ST displacement during an effort, low physical stress tolerance, and heart rhythm disorders. Angiographic criteria include total coronary arterial involvement reaching 75%, intact peripheral channel in all coronary arteries fit for aortocoronary shunting and satisfactory myocardial contractility."},
